%I A401861 #11 Nov 07 2026 23:05:18
%S A401861 1,2,4,7,12,17,23,30,39,48,58,69
%N A401861 Maximum size of a family of distinct subsets of {1, ..., n} whose pairwise intersections are nonempty arithmetic progressions.
%C A401861 Sets with one or two elements count as arithmetic progressions.
%H A401861 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/272">Erdős Problem 272</a>, Erdős Problems.
%F A401861 a(n) >= binomial(n,2) + floor((n-1)/4) + 1.
%Y A401861 Cf. A000125 (the variant allowing empty intersections).
%K A401861 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401861 1,2
%A A401861 _Seiichi Manyama_, Nov 07 2026
